💡 **SUGGESTION: the pair-record snapshot caps only `failureSummary` — the sibling free-text fields (`verifies`, `testPath`) still persist unbounded**

The rework correctly moved the marker-hygiene cap to the snapshot point (`snapshotMemberMeta` → `cappedSnapshotNote` → `tcMaintenanceLedger.truncate`, the ledger's 500-char `MAX_NOTE_LENGTH`) — but it covers exactly one field:

```js
// js/common/tcAlternation.js:250-255
function snapshotMemberMeta(meta) {
    if (!meta) return null;
    var m = deepCopy(meta);
    m.failureSummary = cappedSnapshotNote(m.failureSummary);   // ← only this field
    return m;
}
```

`verifies` comes from `linked.verifies || entry.verifies` (`verifiesOf`, js/postStoryTestAutomationResults.js:978) — linked-TC ticket metadata or agent-copied run-entry text — and `testPath` from the run entry. Both are agent/ticket-authored free text, both are copied verbatim into `registry.pairs[pairKey].members[tcKey]` — the `dmtools:tc-run-registry` marker payload that lives indefinitely until reconciliation — and `conflictMemberLine` (js/common/tcAlternation.js:460) renders `verifies` verbatim into the owner escalation comment.

This is the same vector the `failureSummary` cap closes, for the same cited reason ("agent-authored evidence can be arbitrarily large; the record carries pointers, not essays"). Suggested fix: run `verifies` (and, cheaply, `testPath`) through `cappedSnapshotNote` inside `snapshotMemberMeta` — or keep the cap per-field and carry `failedDescriptionFile` as the pointer. The existing "the member snapshot is marker-hygiene capped" test can assert the second field by passing a long `verifies`.

Non-blocking: realistic `verifies` values are short AC references, so this is payload-hygiene polish, not a defect.

